{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lightsome-sulky-iguanodon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nAGENTS.md (§Git workflow, the bullet at line 235) describes the completion close precheck\ninaccurately, in a way that makes agents believe land-then-close is mechanically enforced when\nit is not.\n\nThe doc says:\n\n> **After the change MERGES, fast-forward YOUR worktree before you close.** The close's\n> completion precheck reads your worktree's git history and requires the merged\n> `rebar-ticket: <id>` commit reachable from HEAD (else it fails with \"cannot confirm the work\n> landed\").\n\nThree things are wrong or missing, verified against the implementation:\n\n1. **\"the merged ... commit\" is wrong.** `_referencing_commit_exists`\n   (src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:149) shells out to `git log --format=%B%x00` with no\n   ref argument and scans HEAD's history for ANY commit carrying a `rebar-ticket:` trailer (or a\n   leading `<id>:` subject) that resolves to the ticket **or any of its transitive descendants**.\n   Merge status is never consulted. An unlanded local commit on your own branch satisfies it.\n\n2. **The precheck is conditional and the doc presents it as unconditional.** It only runs when\n   the ticket records `file_impact` (transition_close.py:283). A ticket with no recorded\n   file_impact never hits this check at all.\n\n3. **`--ref` is not mentioned anywhere in AGENTS.md.** `rebar transition` documents it as:\n   \"Completion close gate: verify (and sign) against the committed tree at <ref> instead of HEAD.\n   Use it to close a stacked story against its own commit while your worktree stays at the epic\n   tip; default HEAD.\" That is precisely the stacked-review workflow this repo uses, and it is the\n   sanctioned alternative to the fast-forward dance the doc presents as mandatory.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe fast-forward advice is a safe superset, so nobody is broken by following it — but the stated\nMECHANISM is false, and agents reason from the mechanism. Believing the precheck enforces\nland-then-close leads to (a) not using `--ref` when closing a stacked story, and (b) asserting to\noperators that pre-land closes are impossible when the only real constraint is the separate,\nadjacent policy rule one bullet above: \"Do not close a ticket until its change is Verified +1 — a\npassing completion-verifier is not a substitute for green CI.\" That policy rule is what actually\norders land-before-close, and it should be the one cited.\n\nThis was hit live: a session told the operator that seven in-progress epic bugs could not be\nclosed before landing because the precheck required merged commits. The operator corrected it.\n\n## Approach\n\nRewrite the bullet so it (a) states the real mechanism — a referencing commit anywhere in the\ncurrent history, ticket or descendant, gated on recorded file_impact; (b) names `--ref` as the\nstacked-close tool; (c) keeps the fast-forward guidance as the remedy for the case it actually\naddresses — a worktree that does NOT contain the commit (a fresh worktree, or closing from a\ncheckout that never had it); and (d) keeps the existing NEVER-touch-the-shared-main-checkout\nwarning verbatim. Cite the Verified +1 policy as the reason to wait, since that is the real one.\n\nDocs-only change. No source behaviour changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: The AGENTS.md bullet no longer claims the precheck requires a MERGED commit.\n- AC2: The bullet states the precheck is conditional on recorded file_impact and that a\n  referencing commit for the ticket OR any transitive descendant satisfies it.\n- AC3: The bullet documents `rebar transition --ref=<ref>` as the way to close a stacked story\n  against its own commit without moving the worktree.\n- AC4: The land-before-close ordering is attributed to the Verified +1 policy rule, not to the\n  precheck.\n- AC5: The NEVER-fast-forward-the-shared-main-checkout warning is preserved.\n- AC6: No source file under src/ is modified; make lint and make typecheck pass.","id":"0c49-c8c9-757f-426d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"AGENTS.md misstates the close precheck: it requires a referencing commit in HEAD's history, not a MERGED one, and omits --ref"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785642540965357001,"uuid":"6de4a92d-08a0-4422-b8d4-df71fd68dfdc"}